e given that one of the components is $2\\mathbf{b}.$ So, we first draw the vector $2\\mathbf{b}$ from the origin. Then we complete the path to the point $C.$\n\n![](images/a8/a8309dc45ac43c6642010e744de5a062d6575d48ba85bd642df39dd261f47422.png)\n\nLet $P$ be the endpoint of the vector $2\\mathbf{b}.$ Then\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{c}=\\overset{\\to }{OP}+\\overset{\\to }{PC}.\n$$\n\nIn $△OPC,$ we have:\n\n- $PC=2|\\mathbf{a}|$\n\n- $\\overset{\\to }{PC}$ and $\\mathbf{a}$ have opposite directions\n\nHence, $\\overset{\\to }{PC}=-2\\mathbf{a}.$\n\nAdditionally,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\mathbf{c} & =\\overset{\\to }{OP}+\\overset{\\to }{PC} \\\\  & =2\\mathbf{b}-2\\mathbf{a}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nConsequently, $\\mathbf{c}=\\lambda \\mathbf{a}+2\\mathbf{b}=-2\\mathbf{a}+2\\mathbf{b}.$\n\nSince $\\mathbf{a}∦\\mathbf{b},$ the linear combination can only be written in one way. Equating the coefficients of $\\mathbf{a},$ we get:\n\n$$\n\\lambda =-2\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186235344 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3cdd0854-261d-5ed4-92ef-477febc75b21" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186234639} {:answer/id #uuid "3eab765d-2302-5205-b5fd-0ada1e027409" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186234642} {:answer/id #uuid "6e5da092-7603-5a36-a455-4137459af1b7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186234713} {:answer/id #uuid "dde73660-f588-5765-aec3-a2559c655608" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186234894} {:answer/id #uuid "e5f2c8c3-d49b-55df-8a1c-5ef41ca2446f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186234905}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e5f2c8c3-d49b-55df-8a1c-5ef41ca2446f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186234905} :answe