}=-3\\mathbf{a}.$\n\nAdditionally,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\mathbf{c} & =\\overset{\\to }{OP}+\\overset{\\to }{PC} \\\\  & =-4\\mathbf{b}-3\\mathbf{a}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nConsequently, $\\mathbf{c}=\\lambda \\mathbf{a}-4\\mathbf{b}=-3\\mathbf{a}-4\\mathbf{b}.$\n\nSince $\\mathbf{a}∦\\mathbf{b},$ the linear combination can only be written in one way. Equating the coefficients of $\\mathbf{a},$ we get:\n\n$$\n\\lambda =-3.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186235566 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c2fb5e87-47ca-5d1c-bf4b-c0767499e5ae" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3/2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186234850}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c2fb5e87-47ca-5d1c-bf4b-c0767499e5ae" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3/2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186234850} :answer-field/id #uuid "845a7492-dbf5-52c7-8f6b-94e8bcddad48" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186235137}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "25a285c7-2943-5076-ba78-0687de680985" :question/math-academy-id "q-325983" :question/problem "![](images/8e/8e6ccf522b5325c3b592ca9470810a95c5491f0b68f000ea774f6555cee0f47f.png)\n\nConsider the picture above. If $\\mathbf{c}=\\lambda \\mathbf{a}-2\\mathbf{b},$ then\n\n$\\lambda =$\n{{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "To find $\\lambda ,$ we want to match the expression\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{c}=\\lambda \\mathbf{a}-2\\mathbf{b}.\n$$\n\nWe are given that one of the components is $-2\\mathbf{b}.$ So, we first draw the vector $-2\\mathbf{b}$ from the origin. Then we complete the path to the point $C.$\n\n![](images/64/646b8f1322f815e786f82eb8cfb3fa9e84a3c8d588c94910b0b702b607bfb2d8.png)\n\nLet $P$ be the endpoint of the vector $-2\\mathbf{b}.$ Then\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{c}=\\overset{\\to }{OP}+\\overset{\\to }{PC}.\n$$\n\nIn $△OPC,$ we have:\n\n- $PC=\\frac{3}{2}|\\mathbf{a}|$\n\n- $\\overset{\\to }{PC}$ and $\\mathbf{a}$ have opposite directions\n\nHence, $\\overset{\\to }{PC}=-\\frac{3}{2}\\mathbf{a}.$\n\nAdditionally,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\mathbf{c} & =\\overset{\\to }{OP}+\\overset{\\to }{PC} \\\\  & =-2\\mathbf{b}-\\frac{3}{2}\\mathbf{a}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nConsequently, $\\mathbf{c}=\\lambda \\mathbf{a}-2\\mathbf{b}=-\\frac{3}{2}\\mathbf{a}-2\\mathbf{b}.$\n\nSince $\\mathbf{a}∦\\mathbf{b},$ the linear combination can only be written in one way. Equating the coefficients of $\\mathbf{a},$ we get:\n\n$$\n\\lambda =-\\frac{3}{2}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186235567 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3d6d4db2-2d84-5cf9-81e1-041f57f2cacc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186234640} {:answer/id #uuid "4a392df7-ad5d-5be9-b18a-e4f744d5c092" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186234660} {:answer/id #uuid "8ed9ea91-ee70-5a16-94a9-6b29294fcbcf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186234766} {:answer/id #uuid "e9b13819-3205-5667-bc39-1375026621c9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186234916} {:answer/id #uuid "fb1af85e-3e3c-595d-9837-0ef51ee523a7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186234942}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fb1af85e-3e3c-595d-9837-0ef51ee523a7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186234942} :answer-field/id #uuid "e877b6bf-02c3-53e5-9ea3-6d64098261ba" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186235250}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "5b87f1b1-b01d-5f2b-86fb-046c3cada5b9" :question/math-academy-id "q-367051" :question/problem "![](images/0f/0f49938e84521acbfe0e44190190ae8b4fe58687a3cc241dbe9f