\\mathbf{c}=\\lambda\\mathbf{a}+2\\mathbf{b}$, find $\\lambda$." :question/worked-solution "First trace $2\\mathbf{b}$ from the common origin $O$ to a point $P$: keep its direction and scale its length. The remaining path from $P$ to the endpoint $C$ must be the unknown multiple of $\\mathbf{a}$.\n\n![](images/d4/d43ce8711cf587ab4552b74961da61f8829f9540d9bab507ee7cf127b6494068.png)\n\nFollowing the grid direction of $\\mathbf{a}$ takes $3$ steps, while the parallel path $PC$ has $3$ steps. Their length ratio is $\\frac{3}{3}=1$. The remaining path points in the opposite direction to $\\mathbf{a}$, so\n$$\n\\overrightarrow{PC}=-\\mathbf{a}.\n$$\nAdding the path vectors gives\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathbf{c}&=\\overrightarrow{OP}+\\overrightarrow{PC}\\\\\n&=2\\mathbf{b}+(-\\mathbf{a})\\\\\n&=-\\mathbf{a}+2\\mathbf{b}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\nBecause $\\mathbf{a}$ and $\\mathbf{b}$ are nonparallel, these coefficients are unique. Comparing with $\\mathbf{c}=\\lambda\\mathbf{a}+2\\mathbf{b}$ gives $\\lambda=-1$. The minus sign records the reversed direction."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186761546 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1f00eade-f4fa-5b6c-8f55-8438c8af9751" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186761522} {:answer/id #uuid "2d06382d-3e17-589c-875a-e6c3ee7a43e6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186761525} {:answer/id #uuid "8e025b38-1ff0-5249-b0bd-4893868e25c1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186761541} {:answer/id #uuid "98118a1b-2fc6-5f31-b4ab-2c0d23f01179" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{7}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186761542} {:answer/id #uuid "aae16f3e-532c-5878-ae0d-b275f139ddac" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186761544}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2d06382d-3e17-589c-875a-e6c3e