thbf{b}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\nBecause $\\mathbf{a}$ and $\\mathbf{b}$ are nonparallel, these coefficients are unique. Comparing with $\\mathbf{c}=\\lambda\\mathbf{a}-4\\mathbf{b}$ gives $\\lambda=-1$. The minus sign records the reversed direction."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186761566 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b303d4d3-ce5c-579b-a1b0-62fcabce16dc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{7}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186761579}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b303d4d3-ce5c-579b-a1b0-62fcabce16dc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{7}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186761579} :answer-field/id #uuid "99d07ee7-8006-57cf-b92d-1ca61d0ec6c9" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186761575}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "6186f711-696a-5694-91f1-4323d8641955" :question/problem "The three vectors share an origin, and each grid square has the same side length.\n\n![](images/b4/b4062187cb72ba000d61cc7c906acda03eb38b8f34bd752344904fdeca809e10.png)\n\nIf $\\mathbf{c}=\\lambda\\mathbf{a}-\\mathbf{b}$, then $\\lambda=$ {{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "First trace $-\\mathbf{b}$ from the common origin $O$ to a point $P$: reverse its direction and scale its length. The remaining path from $P$ to the endpoint $C$ must be the unknown multiple of $\\mathbf{a}$.\n\n![](images/a5/a51afe201aca53375a46ff439b03e2b3f8fec058fb06871aa1398d9dc7e4ebef.png)\n\nFollowing the grid direction of $\\mathbf{a}$ takes $2$ steps, while the parallel path $PC$ has $7$ steps. Their length ratio is $\\frac{7}{2}=\\frac{7}{2}$. The remaining path points in the opposite direction to $\\mathbf{a}$, so\n$$\n\\overrightarrow{PC}=-\\frac{7}{2}\\mathbf{a}.\n$$\nAdding the path vectors gives\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathbf{c}&=\\overrightarrow{OP}+\\overrightarrow{PC}\\\\\n&=-\\mathbf{b}+\\left(-\\frac{7}{2}\\mathbf{a}\\right)\\\\\n&=-\\frac{7}{2}\\mathbf{a}-\\mathbf{b}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\nBecause $\\mathbf{a}$ and $\\mathbf{b}$ are nonparallel, these coefficients are unique. Comparing with $\\mathbf{c}=\\lambda\\mathbf{a}-\\mathbf{b}$ gives $\\lambda=-\\frac{7}{2}$. The minus sign records the reversed direction."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186761568 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "26548894-4d77-5a12-b1e0-9767a6bcb83f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{7}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186761560} {:answer/id #uuid "62ca490e-937f-5b2f-acdb-55a55454599a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{2}{7}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186761567} {:answer/id #uuid "7170a1a0-cab7-5626-9486-eb040433c436" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-14" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186761569} {:answer/id #uuid "c7a07ca7-db83-5ba7-89f0-9a82f2e15bc9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{13}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186761581} {:answer/id #uuid "caf095a4-1747-502c-85f0-c5158809d818" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{14}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186761582}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "26548894-4d77-5a12-b1e0-9767a6bcb83f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{7}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186761560} :answer-field/id #uuid "9177891f-10c6-5718-a67e-32c7ea4dbe75" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186761573}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "6423178c-2eaf-5332-9d49-4298e72d771d" :question/problem "The three vectors share an origin, and each grid square has the same side length.\n\n![](images/d0/d0781081331f88d9c1cbc54562e3d2b027b9f15eceec4acb2015f24e7709f9b8.png)\n\nGiven $\\mathbf{c}=\\lambda\\mathbf{a}-3\\mathbf{b}$, find $\\lambda$." :question/worked-solution "First trace $-3\\mat